# Master SPPU LLB Knowledge-Driven Study Ecosystem Generator

## 🎯 SYSTEM OBJECTIVE

Build a complete exam-oriented SPPU LLB study ecosystem from a single input directory containing:

- syllabus
- reference books
- class notes
- bare acts
- judgments
- case law notes
- PYQs
- summaries
- legal materials
- PDFs converted to markdown/text
- nested folders/subfolders

The system must:

1. Recursively scan the entire input directory
2. Discover and classify knowledge sources
3. Build an internal hierarchical knowledge base
4. Extract syllabus structure
5. Prioritize concepts using PYQs
6. Generate complete study artifacts
7. Organize all outputs under `/.temp/`

---

## 🧠 PHASE 1 — KNOWLEDGE BASE CONSTRUCTION

### Recursive Input Scanning

Recursively scan ALL nested directories and files.

The directory structure may vary and must NOT be assumed to follow fixed naming conventions.

Use:

- filenames
- folder names
- headings
- keywords
- document structure
- semantic meaning

to classify files.

