## 📂 MULTI-FILE OUTPUT RULE

Generated study material MUST match the **SPPU LLB Subject Folder Pack** layout. **In-repo reference:** `Academics/Law/SPPU/LLB - I/Semester - 2/Constitutional Law - II/` (deep `01-complete-notes`, per-module `02-condensed-notes` EXAM_READY files, `03-visual-aids` with Mind_Maps / Flowcharts / Comparison_Tables, `04-case-laws`, mark-sliced `05-question-bank` with **one question per file** and **full model answers in-file**, root `README.md`, `NAVIGATION_INDEX.md`, `📖_START_HERE.md`, `07-quick-revision`, `08-exam-strategy`, `09-practice-worksheets`).

### Mandatory rule stack

- **`sppu-llb-subject-folder-pack`** — folder tree `00–09`, naming (`Module_<NN>_...`, `Q###_...`, `D###_...`), navigation, mark buckets, distinguishers.
- **`sppu-llb-topper-generator-ultimate`** — definition-first answers, hybrid body, case blocks, mark-based length inside notes and question files.

### Where to write

- Default staging: **`/.temp/<Subject-Slug>-subject-pack/`** (full tree).
- Write under `Academics/.../<Subject>/` only when the user explicitly allows replacing or extending an existing pack.

### Forbidden (shallow ecosystem)

- Only `knowledge-base/` + one outline, or README-only trees.
- Single “all modules” stub without **per-module** `01-complete-notes` and **per-module** `02-condensed-notes` EXAM_READY files.
- Question bank as one markdown per module instead of **mark folders + one file per question + model answer**.

---

## 📁 OUTPUT STRUCTURE (subject folder pack)

Under the output root, implement at least:

- **`00-syllabus-and-references/`** — syllabus; pointers or copies for acts / PYQs used.
- **`01-complete-notes/`** — **one long-form file per syllabus module:** `Module_<NN>_<Descriptive_Title>.md` (paragraphs, selective bullets, tables, case blocks: short facts → issue → holding → principle → article or section link).
- **`02-condensed-notes/`** — **one EXAM_READY file per module:** `Module_<NN>_<Short_Label>_EXAM_READY.md` with Quick Stats, “What This Covers”, **COUNT** lists, mnemonics, exam trigger lines.
- **`03-visual-aids/`** — `Mind_Maps/`, `Flowcharts/`, `Comparison_Tables/`; target **≥1 visual artifact per module** where syllabus supports it.
- **`04-case-laws/`** — `Landmark_Cases_Summary.md` and `Module_Wise_Cases/Module_<NN>_..._Cases.md` per module as needed.
- **`05-question-bank/`** — `2_Marks/`, `5_Marks/`, `10_Marks/`, `15_Marks/`; `Q<###>_<Title>.md` each with question metadata + **`## MODEL ANSWER`** section; `Distinguish_Between/`; `Topic_Weightage_and_Focus_Map.md`; probable-questions file (e.g. `Most_Probable_Questions_Next_Exam.md`). Respect `.markdownlint-cli2.yaml` if present under `05-question-bank/`.
- **`07-quick-revision/`** — e.g. `Last_Hour_Checklist.md`, `All_Mnemonics_One_Page.md`, topic quick refs.
- **`08-exam-strategy/`** — answer writing template + common mistakes (minimum).
- **`09-practice-worksheets/`** — **≥2** practice tests spanning modules.

### Root docs (mandatory)

- **`README.md`**, **`NAVIGATION_INDEX.md`**, **`📖_START_HERE.md`** (or `START_HERE.md`).

Optional `06-model-answers/` or `07-previous-papers/` — use only if populated; else one-line `README.md` stating unused.

---

## 🧩 AUTO TOPIC SPLITTING

- **Complete notes:** one file **per syllabus module** (Constitutional Law II style), not one thin spine for the whole course unless the user explicitly asks for outline-only.
- **Condensed:** one **EXAM_READY** file **per module**, paired with `01-complete-notes/`.
- **Question bank:** **one file per question** in the correct mark folder; each file includes a **full** model answer for that mark range; no mixing unrelated topics in one question file.
- **No topic mixing** in single-topic artifacts; cross-topic only in worksheets or stated revision aggregates.

